# Critical Rules

## Summary

This document defines critical rules that must always be followed during development. It covers:

- **Critical Restrictions**: Never create .md files or run destructive commands without approval, never modify translations without permission
- **Development Workflow**: Pre-commit checklist, code standards, and testing requirements
- **Database Guidelines**: Safe schema changes and verification practices
- **Security & Performance**: NextAuth.js, error boundaries, environment variables, query optimization
- **Current Features**: Overview of existing application features

These rules take precedence over all other guidelines. Always follow the pre-commit checklist and use static analysis tools before committing.

## 🚫 CRITICAL RULES

- ❌ NEVER create .md files, READMEs, or run commands without approval (except plans/PRDs under `.cursor/plans/` and `/to-issues` slices under `.scratch/`)
- ❌ NEVER modify translation files without explicit permission
- ❌ NEVER add new styles without explicit user approval (see Styling below)
- ❌ NEVER add, expand, or update tests unless the user explicitly asks for tests
- ❌ NEVER run `npx prisma db push --force-reset` or `npx prisma migrate dev`
- ❌ NEVER run `npm run dev` or any development server commands automatically
- ✅ Use `search_replace` with 3-5 lines context, `read_file`, `grep_search`
- ✅ Use static analysis: `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run test:unit`, `npm run lint`

## 🏗️ Development Workflow

### Pre-Commit Checklist

1. Remove development logs (console.log, debug, info)
2. Keep only error logging and critical failures
3. Remove commented code, unused variables, outdated TODOs

### Styling (requires explicit approval for new styles)

- **Default**: Reuse existing theme — `app/theme/components.ts`, `app/theme/toolbarStyles.ts`, MUI `data-hebrew` variants, `endless-scroll-toolbar`, `ToolbarDropdownFilter`, `input-toolbar-labeled`, and component layout props (`fullWidth`, `dir`, `slotProps`) — before adding anything new
- ❌ Do **not** add new global theme blocks, new CSS class hooks (e.g. feature-specific `#id` or one-off class names in `MuiCssBaseline`), duplicated `sx` style objects, or new entries in `toolbarStyles.ts` / `components.ts` unless the user explicitly approves
- ✅ Allowed without asking: wiring existing classes (e.g. `endless-scroll-toolbar`, `data-hebrew`), minimal layout-only `sx` (flex, gap, width on a single component), and extending an **existing** theme selector when the user asked to fix styling using the theme
- If existing theme cannot cover the case, **stop and ask** before inventing new styles

### Code Standards

- Use TypeScript, proper error handling, React Query
- Use NextAuth.js with role-based access control
- Create feature branches, review before merging
- Write or update tests only when the user explicitly asks
- **When generating plans**: Always include a Testing Strategy section with test units mapped to business requirements (see Testing Guidelines)

### Database Guidelines

- Check Prisma schema before creating scripts
- Never assume field names - verify in schema
- Test scripts with small data subsets
- Use `npx prisma db push` for safe schema changes

## 🔒 Security & Performance

- Use NextAuth.js with role-based access control
- Implement error boundaries and user-friendly error messages
- Use environment variables for sensitive information
- Optimize queries, use proper indexing and pagination

## 📋 Current Features

- User, Customer, Invoice, Activity, Dispute management
- Collection period tracking, Multi-language support, Role-based access control
